<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104270" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τον-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for stretching, capable of extension,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρνιθες κατὰ πτέρυγας τονικοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>PA</u>
					693b12
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Mus.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ τονικὸν [χρῶμα</span>] (opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἡμιτόνιον</span> (fort. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμιόλιον,</span> cf. <i><span class="en">
				Cleonid.
				<u>Harm.</u>
				7
			</span></i>) and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ μαλακόν</span>), one of
			the three forms of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρῶμα</span> or
			chromatic scale, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				6.51
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>of</i> or <i>for accents,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τονικὰ παραγγέλματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.D.
					<u>Adv.</u>
					181.9
				</span></i>
			 (so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ τ. π.,</span> treatise by Jo.<i><span class="en">
				Alex.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ -κόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.D.
					<u>Pron.</u>
					35.13
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>resulting from</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.4
				</span></i>
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κίνησις,</span> of God, opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεταβατικῶς κινούμενος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				2.149
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				147
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			<i>contractile,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνέργεια,</span> of a muscle, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				4.436
			</span></i>; [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέπερι] στομάχου -ώτερον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					6.265
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					4.435
				</span></i>
			.</div>
